      "writtenOn": "2023-12-21T02:48:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Greg.\nThank you for reviewing.\n\nDoes the \"mainline branch\" you said mean the \"aosp/android-mainline\" ?\n\n\"vendor hook\" is a specific feature of ACK and is not in the Kernel Mainline.\nI agree that error handling or general functions related to this subsystem should be worked on the kernel mainline.\nHowever, I understand that functions that the OEM needs can be implemented using \"vendor hook\".",
      "parentUuid": "cc4beb66_e2a13d0c",
      "revId": "e4eadab7fc2baa0be33e4b6689342fce96507a2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "793dda8a_1f955468",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-21T11:47:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please work to get the needed changes for proper error handling and other functionality merged to the upstream kernel.org releases, do not rely on vendor-hooks as that is not going to be the way forward, AND we can not keep taking them for forever.",
      "parentUuid": "8e4beb84_c26dbeba",
      "revId": "e4eadab7fc2baa0be33e4b6689342fce96507a2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3422fca9_f361b2a0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3233542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T04:58:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Greg,\n\nMany vendors have used vendor hook funtions in other drivers as well as mmc driver and managed some confidential and vendor-specific codes in them until android14-5.15. But the vh functions is not merged from android14-6.1, we are having difficulty managing the code using the vh functions. We would like to ask if you should at least maintain backward compatibility. We do not want to add new vh function, just ask to maintain the existing vh functions. Please do not repeat speaking upstream, consider each vendor\u0027s difficulties in managing confidential \u0026 vendor-specific codes which can\u0027t be upstream. That is why the vh functions exist.\n\nWe don\u0027t think requesting backward compatibility is a difficult requirement. \nWe look forward to positive feedback.\n\nThanks.",
      "revId": "e4eadab7fc2baa0be33e4b6689342fce96507a2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18501535_def8bc6f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T08:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do NOT maintain backwards compatibility with vendor hooks at all, they need to be justified for each new kernel version, as always.\n\nPlease work to get your needed changes upstream, we can not take vendor hooks for forever without this work happening, that is not what vendor hooks are for at all.",
      "parentUuid": "3422fca9_f361b2a0",
      "revId": "e4eadab7fc2baa0be33e4b6689342fce96507a2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8962bb3a_20c8a371",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3233542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-22T09:04:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But As we know, vh functions of ufs driver which we are developing are merged to android mainline, they are merged to the latest android kernel branch automatically. So the vh functions of ufs driver support backward compatibility.\n\n\u003c\u003c gerrit link which Google engineer merged vendor hooks to android mainline \u003e\u003e\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/1611216\n\nWhy are you inconsistent with vendor hook management policy?\nIt would be nice if all drivers had consistent management policies of vh functions.\n\nCan\u0027t you manage the existing vh functions of the mmc driver in the same way as the ufs driver?",
      "parentUuid": "18501535_def8bc6f",
      "revId": "e4eadab7fc2baa0be33e4b6689342fce96507a2d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
